# Problem Statement

> **"Youtube has billions of videos. When a user wants certain videos to watch, without recommendation system, it fails to fulfill the pin point of the user. So, in 2008, Youtube launched its recommendation system which was further advanced as **user-based collaborative filtering."** **

## Impact of YouTube Recommendation System

**1. Impact on Users**

* Personalized video recommendations
* Faster content discovery
* Better user experience
* Increased engagement
* Helps users discover new creators and topics

**2. Impact on Database/Data**

* Generates large amounts of user-behavior data
* Stores watch history, likes, searches, and preferences
* Helps build user-interest profiles
* Requires scalable storage and data processing
* Creates privacy and data-security requirements

**3. Impact on Overall System**

* Makes YouTube more personalized and useful
* Requires scalable APIs, databases, and recommendation infrastructure
* Helps creators reach relevant audiences
* Creates a continuous feedback loop:

```
User Activity
```

     ↓

Data Collection

     ↓

Recommendation

     ↓

User Interaction

     ↓

More Data

     ↓

Better Recommendation

